    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d275-a2">

                <pb facs="0731" n="641" xml:id="pg641"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 25.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Derby to Mr.
                            Hoffman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-08-26"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 26,
                        1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 24th instant, together with its inclosures, conveying the
                    thanks of your Government, through that of Her Majesty, to the authorities and
                    people of New Zealand, for the courteous and hospitable reception accorded by
                    them to the American expedition sent to that colony to observe the transit of
                    Venus, and I have to state to you, in reply, that I have referred your note to
                    the proper department of Her Majesty’s government.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, sir, your most obedient, humble
                    servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>DERBY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Colonel <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hoffman</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
